houlders, head, knees, fingers, expression, and hair response copy the source performance without enlarging or multiplying any movement.\n\nFrom 00:10.250 to 00:12.250, her hands lower and reset on the same frames, then one index finger rises beside the face and points toward the camera as her torso turns to the same slight three-quarter angle. The hand retracts into the same paired open-palm shapes in front of the chest while her gaze and expression track the source dancer exactly.\n\nFrom 00:12.250 to 00:13.250, one arm follows the source diagonal arc above the head while the other opens down and outward, reaching the widest pose only at the matching source moment. She holds it for the same duration and returns along the same path.\n\nFrom 00:13.250 to 00:15.125, she performs the same shoulder-level wave, lowers both hands, then lifts them from waist to shoulder height and raises both forearms on the final beat. The ending lands on the exact source frame: both hands form matching V-signs beside the eyes, the eyes close in the same cheerful expression, and one lower leg bends backward to the same height and angle. The final pose receives only the source hold through 00:15.125, with the clip ending immediately on the matching frame.\n\nThroughout [Shot 1], <Subject 2> remains temporally locked to <Video 1>: preserve each action's count, start frame, end frame, velocity curve, range, direction, pause, and overlap. Hair and fabric respond only to those inherited movements. <Subject 1>'s identity and athletic school outfit remain stable through occlusion and motion, with the shirt, separate shorts, socks, and sneakers consistently reconstructed. <Subject 3> fills the frame continuously. The lower-right background is reconstructed cleanly and seamlessly after removing every source watermark, logo, username, and overlay mark. <Audio 1> plays in sample-accurate synchronization for the full shot.\n\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A\n"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "n